,000 due to delays and extra work","detail":"Playground improvements project that rolled forward from 2025/26 finished in early 2026 but incurred additional costs beyond the rolled-forward budget allowance.","category":"overspend","matters":"Scheme-level cost overrun; demonstrates budget planning and/or contingency issues","figures":"\u00a337,000 overspend","quote":"due to delays and extra work required the final costs have exceeded the budget by \u00a337,000.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring 2026-27 July","paper_url":"https://dartford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s82171/82171.pdf","headline":"General Fund capital budget reduced by \u00a30.197m due to 2025/26 overspend, constraining current year","detail":"The 2026/27 General Fund capital budget was set at \u00a337.579m but has been reduced by \u00a30.197m as a result of overspending in 2025/26, bringing the revised budget to \u00a338.044m after additions (museum redesign and Stone Parish grant).","category":"overspend","matters":"Prior year capital overspending reduces flexibility in current year; indicates cost control issues carry forward","figures":"\u00a30.197m reduction in budget","quote":"The budget approved by GAC on 23 February 2026 was \u00a337.579m. The budget for 2026-27 has been reduced by \u00a30.197m as a result of the 2025-26 overspend.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring 2026-27 July","paper_url":"https://dartford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s82171/82171.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation purchase programme to be unfunded, increasing Capital Financing Requirement by \u00a34.13m","detail":"\u00a34.13m of temporary accommodation capital expenditure (property purchases) is expected to be unfunded this year, driving an increase in the council's borrowing requirement (CFR). The council will set aside Minimum Revenue Provision over the life of the properties to fund debt repayment.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Council taking on new capital debt to fund homelessness provision; increases debt service obligations and CFR trajectory","figures":"\u00a34.13m unfunded capital spend","quote":"\u00a34.13m of expenditure on temporary accommodation units is expected to be unfunded during the year, thereby increasing the Council's Capital Financing Requirement (CFR). The Council will set aside Minimum Revenue Provision (MRP) over the life of the houses to fund the purchases.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring 2026-27 July","paper_url":"https://dartford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s82171/82171.pdf","headline":"DTCR Phase 3A Spital Street works expanded after subsurface concrete discovery during construction","detail":"Concrete found under the carriageway was not identified in early site investigations. Kent County Council as highways authority required excavation and carriageway reconstruction, increasing scope, working hours, and traffic management complexity. Work expected to complete end July.","category":"capital","matters":"Subsurface discovery increases project costs and complexity; demonstrates risk in early site investigation and project delivery","figures":"Amount of cost increase not stated","quote":"The scope of work has expanded as concrete was found under the carriageway which had not shown up in early site investigations. As highways authority, Kent County Council have required the concrete to be excavated and the carriageway reconstructed.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring 2026-27 July","paper_url":"https://dartford.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s82171/82171.pdf","headline":"Dartford Football Club roof insulation found in worse condition than expected, requiring budget revision","detail":"During planned sedum roof removal works, moisture mapping revealed insulation in a worsened condition. The council is obtaining estimates for more complex rectification and will report on cost and revised budget by early August. This is described as necessary work requiring capital budget increase.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital project discovered to be significantly more expensive than anticipated; budget forecasting accuracy and cost control risk","figures":"Budget revision expected; amount not yet quantified","quote":"the Council have these results which show a worsened condition than hoped or expected. The property team are obtaining estimates for a more complex rectification and will report on cost and budget in early August. The work will be necessary and a revision to this capital budget is expected to be required.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-28"},"name":"Dartford","findings_total":41,"news_drafts_total":3}}